2.0.1:
[Fix] state_bans_active_remove/state_events_prune: restore 600 permissions on
      state files after awk rewrite (temp file inherits umask, not original perms)
[New] elog_lib.sh: shared structured logging library (v1.0.0) with severity
      levels (debug/info/warn/error/critical), classic syslog-style and JSON
      (JSONL) output formats, configurable via ELOG_* variables
[New] conf.bfd: LOG_FORMAT (classic/json) and LOG_LEVEL (0-4) variables for
      structured logging control
[Change] eout()/vout(): rewritten as thin wrappers delegating to elog library;
      format-identical output preserves full backward compatibility
[Change] ~29 log calls in bfd.lib.sh and bfd assigned explicit severity levels
      (error for failures, warn for degraded/skipped, info for normal operations)
[Change] update-ipcountry.sh: download timeout (120s default, DL_TIMEOUT var),
      TLS fallback with warning for legacy CA bundles, temp files in
      INSTALL_PATH/tmp instead of /tmp, INSTALL_PATH uses ${:-} default
[Fix] install.sh: update-ipcountry.sh now chmod 750 (was 640 from blanket) and
      included in custom INSTALL_PATH sed replacement list
[Change] check(): per-cycle caching for ip_to_country (eliminates repeated awk
      scans of 190K-line ipcountry.dat), pre-built ignore list cache (single
      grep vs per-IP file re-reads), pre-computed IP occurrence counts via
      uniq -c (O(n log n) vs O(n^2) grep in record_and_score)
[New] _build_ignore_cache(): merges all ignore files into single comment-stripped
      file for O(1) per-IP lookup during detection cycles
[Note] F-066 (pressure_compute per-IP awk) deferred — events.dat is 10-100x
      smaller than country DB; batching requires loop restructuring
[Note] F-067 (state_bans_active_check per-IP) — false positive in practice;
      bans.active is small and only checked for threshold-tripping IPs
[Fix] filter_host: inline comments after IPs in ignore files now handled
      correctly; grep -v "#" replaced with sed comment-strip pipeline
[Fix] ip_to_subnet: added defensive guard for subnet masks below /8
[Fix] _load_pressure_conf: PRESSURE_WEIGHT and PRESSURE_TRIP values now
      type-validated; non-numeric or zero values logged and skipped
[Note] F-018 (pam_generic/sshd overlap) verified as intentional design
[Note] F-033 (-b SERVICE validation) verified as correct — freeform label
[Fix] CI: shellcheck lint step now uses -S warning to filter info/style
      noise; inline shellcheck directives added for 8 known false positives
      in bfd.lib.sh (template vars consumed by sourced alert.bfd, read
      placeholders, mkdir -m with -p where parent always exists)
[Fix] CI: added files/tlog_lib.sh to shellcheck lint targets
[Fix] tests/28-install-paths.bats: updated for tlog rewrite — files/tlog no
      longer contains /usr/local/bfd (uses relative path to tlog_lib.sh);
      removed tlog from INSPATH sed replacement tests to match install.sh
[Fix] bfd.lib.sh: removed unused local variable 'expired_line' from
      process_unbans()
[Change] tlog functions extracted to shared tlog_lib.sh library; tlog_read(),
      tlog_journal_filter(), tlog_journal_read() and 4 internal helpers replaced
      by canonical tlog_lib.sh (sourced at bfd.lib.sh load time)
[New] tlog_journal_register(): 23 BFD service-to-journalctl filter mappings
      migrated from hardcoded case statement to dynamic registry
[New] atomic cursor writes (mktemp+mv) for all tlog operations; replaces
      non-atomic echo-redirect pattern
[New] optional flock-based cursor locking enabled in watch mode (TLOG_FLOCK=1);
      prevents concurrent access between watch daemon and cron.daily
[New] cursor validation with auto-reset on corruption (exit code 2)
[New] multi-mode tracking support (bytes default, lines selectable per call)
[New] stale cursor protection: mtime updated on every tlog_read call
[New] configurable first-run behavior (TLOG_FIRST_RUN=skip|full)
[New] tlog_adjust_cursor() for mode-aware in-place log trim support
[Change] files/tlog replaced with tlog_lib standalone wrapper (sources
      tlog_lib.sh instead of reimplementing tracking logic)
[Fix] tlog BASERUN: install.sh replaces default /tmp with $INSPATH/tmp at
      install time; prevents cursor files from defaulting to world-writable
      /tmp; source tree keeps canonical /tmp for cross-project hash parity
[Change] tlog_lib.sh: update to canonical 2.0.1 with multi-format compressed
      rotation (.xz, .bz2, .zst, .lz4), copytruncate rotation handling, mode
      validation in tlog_read(), and generic decompression dispatch
[Change] tlog: update to canonical 2.0.1 CLI with option parsing (-m/--mode,
      -b/--baserun, -f/--flock, --first-run), subcommands (--full, --status,
      --reset, --adjust), help system (-v/-h/--help), path traversal rejection,
      and library security validation; backward-compatible positional interface
[New] tests/03-validate-rule.bats: 8 _compat_rule_vars() unit tests covering
      all 4 legacy→canonical mappings, preservation semantics when new names
      already set, empty old names, and mixed old/new resolution
[Fix] show_status(): add missing _compat_rule_vars() call after sourcing rule
      files; old-style rules using REQ instead of PREREQ were incorrectly
      counted as inactive in status output
[Fix] show_rule(), test_rule(): reorder _compat_rule_vars() before
      _apply_pressure() for consistency with check() and _hc_rules() call
      order; no functional change (variable sets are non-overlapping)
[Change] tests: relocate 10 misplaced tests to logical home files —
      extract_command_template (4 tests) from 09-state-io to 22-alert-format;
      _hc_config (1 test) from 04-config-validation to 23-health-check;
      _save/_restore/_clear_rule_vars and _rule_is_active (5 tests) from
      04-config-validation to 03-validate-rule
[New] README, README.md, bfd.1: upgrade documentation section covering
      importconf migration, config variable renames, state preservation,
      post-upgrade verification, and rollback procedure
[Fix] state_init(): enforce 750 permissions on tmp/ and stats/ directories
      (mkdir -m 750); previously relied on pre() to set permissions, leaving an
      unprotected window if state_init() was called independently
[Fix] validate_config(): reject SCAN_TIMEOUT=0; GNU timeout 0 means "no timeout"
      which could cause journalctl to hang indefinitely during scan mode
[Fix] watch(): SIGTERM/SIGINT now properly exit the daemon; previous trap
      pattern ran cleanup_watch but let the while-true loop continue; changed
      to EXIT-only cleanup with separate TERM/INT traps that call exit
[Fix] reload_watch(): unset config vars BEFORE re-sourcing conf.bfd, not
      after; previous ordering destroyed freshly-sourced values so config
      changes (e.g., PRESSURE_TRIP) never took effect on SIGHUP reload
[New] tests/33-watch-mode.bats: 15 tests for watch mode daemon lifecycle;
      10 unit tests (cleanup_watch lock removal/logging, reload_watch config
      re-sourcing/safety-rejection/pressure-array-clearing/fallback-derivation);
      5 integration tests (lock creation, PID file, start logging, SIGTERM
      graceful shutdown, SIGHUP config reload)
[Fix] reload_watch(): clear pressure arrays (_PRESS_WEIGHT/_TRIP/_SKIP_ALERT/
      _RULE_EMAIL) before reload; if pressure.conf is deleted while daemon
      runs, stale arrays no longer persist from previous load
[Fix] reload_watch(): add full fallback variable block matching startup
      lines 90-100 (RULES_PATH, TLOG_PATH, EMAIL_TEMPLATE, etc.); defends
      against config-sourcing failures leaving variables unset
[Fix] importconf: preserve tlog byte-offset state files on upgrade; loop
      copies bare-name files (sshd, dovecot, postfix, etc.) from old tmp/,
      skipping dotfiles and extension files already handled by other cp's
[Fix] importconf: preserve user's custom alert.bfd template on upgrade;
      install.sh unconditionally overwrites with new default, importconf
      now restores from backup if present
[Fix] show_config(): replace eval-based variable indirection with ${!var}
      indirect expansion; eliminates eval from display path while preserving
      whitelist validation and BAN_COMMAND case mapping
[Fix] quiet mode (-q): remove stderr redirect so genuine errors from tlog
      functions reach cron's mail handler; stdout suppression sufficient for
      cron silence since eout() writes to log file regardless
[New] tests: direct test coverage for sanitize_ports() (12 cases) and
      expand_command_template() (7 cases) — security-critical input validation
      and safe template expansion functions
[Fix] cron.daily: check mkdir-based lock (lock.utime.lk) before rotating state
      files; prevents racing with running bfd process that uses directory-based
      locking; flock retained for self-contention between cron.daily invocations
[Fix] _fw_iptables_ban/_fw_iptables_unban: guard against empty $_FW_IP6T_BIN
      when ip6tables is not installed; IPv6 bans now log a warning and return 1
      instead of executing an empty command; _fw_iptables_setup logs one-time
      warning when ip6tables is missing
[Fix] README: corrected watch mode lock description from "flock" to "atomic
      directory creation" to match actual mkdir-based implementation
[New] GitHub Actions release workflow (.github/workflows/release.yml): builds
      RPM (el7, el8, el9, el10) and DEB packages in parallel Docker containers
      on v* tag push; creates GitHub Release with all packages as assets
[New] RPM packaging (pkg/rpm/bfd.spec): FHS-compliant layout with files at
      /usr/sbin, /usr/lib/bfd, /etc/bfd, /usr/share/bfd, /var/lib/bfd;
      symlink farm at /usr/local/bfd for backward compatibility; sed transforms
      at build time for internals.conf, cron, systemd units; %config(noreplace)
      for all user-editable config; install.sh migration in %pre/%post;
      single spec covers el7/el8/el9/el10
[New] DEB packaging (pkg/deb/debian/): FHS layout with dh_link-based symlink
      farm; debhelper-compat 13; conffile protection; preinst/postinst handle
      install.sh-to-package migration; single .deb covers Debian 12 and
      Ubuntu 18/20/22/24
[New] Package build infrastructure (pkg/Makefile): source tarball via git
      archive; native rpm/deb targets; Docker build containers for el7
      (CentOS 7), el9 (Rocky 9, covers el8/el9/el10), and Debian 12;
      test-rpm-rocky9 and test-deb-debian12 targets for install verification
[New] Package verification test suite (pkg/test/test-pkg-install.sh): 10 test
      categories covering FHS paths, symlink farm, internals.conf transforms,
      lock coordination, cron paths, permissions, rule files, exclude.files,
      systemd units, and bfd execution via both /usr/sbin and /usr/local/sbin
[Fix] stat -c calls in bfd, bfd.lib.sh, tlog: add -L flag to dereference
      symlinks before checking ownership/permissions; required for package
      installs where /usr/local/bfd/ files are symlinks to FHS locations;
      backward-compatible (no-op on regular files for install.sh installs)
[New] README (plain text): section 5.7 Scan Mode with use cases, CLI examples,
      safety limits, and lock behavior; --scan/--max-lines=/--scan-timeout= in
      CLI usage block; SCAN_MAX_LINES/SCAN_TIMEOUT in 3.7 Advanced config;
      TOC entry for section 5.7
[Change] install.sh: contextual progress output for every blocking stage;
      plain-English verbs with no prefix sigils; echo-n/done on stop/start
      so systemctl calls are never a silent pause; stage markers (header,
      backing up, installing, importing); summary block with 2-space indent
[Fix] install.sh: stop watch mode before upgrade to avoid 15s restart delay
      and stray output from dying process; new _stop_services() called before
      backup(); _enable_services() uses start instead of restart
[New] 32-scan.bats: 48 tests covering _tlog_read_full, _tlog_journal_read_full,
      _tlog_advance_scan_cursors, _rule_tlog scan branch, check() scan mode
      integration, cursor advancement, CLI argument parsing, validate_config,
      and show_config for scan variables (974 total tests, 0 failures)
[New] bfd.1: Scan Mode subsection with --scan, --max-lines=, --scan-timeout=;
      SCAN_MAX_LINES and SCAN_TIMEOUT in Advanced config section
[New] README: section 5.7 Scan Mode with usage, use cases, safety limits,
      and lock behavior; SCAN_MAX_LINES/SCAN_TIMEOUT in 3.7 Advanced table
[Change] bfd.bash-completion: --scan, --max-lines=, --scan-timeout= in long
      flags; --scan context completes rule names; config_vars updated
[New] --scan CLI option: scan full logs for all rules or a specific rule;
      supports -d/--dryrun, --max-lines=N, --scan-timeout=N; acquires lock,
      runs check() in scan mode, advances cursors after non-dry-run scan
[New] SCAN_MAX_LINES and SCAN_TIMEOUT config variables in conf.bfd Advanced
      section with validate_config() and show_config() support
[New] scan mode core: _tlog_read_full(), _tlog_journal_read_full(), and
      _tlog_advance_scan_cursors() for full-log processing without cursor tracking;
      _rule_tlog() scan branch; check() rule filter and cursor pair collection;
      summary label distinguishes "scan complete" from "run complete"
[Change] weights.country renamed to pressure-country.conf; PRESSURE_COUNTRY
      toggle removed — country weighting is now auto-enabled when
      pressure-country.conf has uncommented entries; removes config variable
      from conf.bfd, validate_config(), show_config(), and bash completion
[Fix] tlog_journal_read: unquote $jfilter so multi-filter entries (exim OR
      syntax) are word-split into separate journalctl arguments; single-filter
      entries unaffected; shellcheck SC2086 suppressed with safety comment
[Change] dovecot rule: AUTH_LOG_PATH fallback when MAIL_LOG_PATH missing
      (Debian/Ubuntu systems where dovecot logs to auth.log)
[Change] exim_authfail/exim_nxuser rules: Debian support — /usr/sbin/exim4
      binary fallback, /var/log/exim4/mainlog log path fallback
[Change] asterisk_badauth/asterisk_iax/asterisk_nopeer rules: /var/log/
      asterisk/messages fallback when /var/log/asterisk/full missing
[Change] http_401 rule: conservative defaults enabled (PRESSURE_WEIGHT=1,
      PRESSURE_TRIP=60) to prevent false positives from legitimate 401s
[Change] pam_generic rule: conservative defaults enabled (PRESSURE_WEIGHT=1,
      PRESSURE_TRIP=40) with overlap documentation comment
[Change] validate_rule() rewritten to distinguish inactive rules (silent skip)
      from genuine misconfigurations (logged); PREREQ-missing and file-detection
      with no match are now silent; MATCHED_HOSTS check moved to caller
[Change] check() output: "processing rule file" messages now verbose-only;
      new summary format "N active rules, M with events, P events parsed,
      K bans executed"; active_count tracks rules passing validate_rule
[New] tlog_journal_filter() expanded from 16 to 23 entries: openvpn,
      exim_authfail, exim_nxuser, xrdp, asterisk, asterisk.iax, asterisk_nopeer
[Change] rule variables renamed for clarity: REQ→PREREQ, LP→LOG_FILE,
      TLOG_TF→LOG_TAG, ARG_VAL→MATCHED_HOSTS; all 42 rule files, library
      functions, and diagnostics updated; _compat_rule_vars() shim provides
      full backward compatibility for custom rules using old names
[New] install.sh: auto-enable watch mode on fresh install (systemd + SysVinit);
      upgrades respect existing timer/watch choice
[Change] install.sh: cleaner post-install output reflecting active scheduling mode
[Change] README: sections 2, 2.1, Quick Start updated for auto-enabled watch mode
[Change] bfd.1: DESCRIPTION updated to reflect watch mode as default on install
[New] proxmox rule: pvedaemon/pveproxy authentication failure via PAM
[New] lighttpd rule: mod_auth password mismatch with dynamic log detection
[New] mongodb rule: authentication failed from client
[New] xrdp rule: AUTHFAIL and pam_authenticate failed
[New] openvpn rule: TLS Auth Error, VERIFY ERROR, TLS handshake failed
      (community edition; separate from openvpnas Access Server rule)
[New] phpmyadmin rule: mysql-denied and user denied via syslog
      (requires AuthLog='syslog' in phpMyAdmin config)
[New] gitlab rule: Failed Login from application.log
[New] grafana rule: invalid username or password with remote_addr
[Change] sshd rule expanded from 3 to 8 patterns: keyboard-interactive, ident
      string, refused connect, max auth attempts, PAM failure (LFD/fail2ban)
[Change] dovecot rule expanded from 2 to 5 patterns: Disconnected pop3/imap,
      submission-login auth failed
[Change] proftpd rule expanded from 1 to 4 patterns: incorrect password,
      SECURITY VIOLATION, maximum login attempts
[Change] exim_authfail rule expanded from 1 to 3 patterns: dovecot_*
      authenticator, SMTP protocol synchronization error
[Change] asterisk_badauth rule expanded from 1 to 2 patterns: SecurityEvent
      FailedACL (Asterisk 12+ security framework)
[Change] postfix PORTS updated from 25,26 to 25,26,587,465 (submission/SMTPS)
[Change] sendmail rule expanded from 1 to 2 patterns: AUTH failure
[New] tests/regex_samples.txt: data-driven test corpus covering all 42 rules
      with positive and negative test cases; RFC 5737 IP compliant; data-driven
      BATS tests in 13-regex-samples.bats validate all samples automatically
[Change] conf.bfd restructured into workflow-oriented sections (Pressure Model,
      Email Alerts, Banning, Custom Firewall Commands, Log Paths, Advanced);
      comments rewritten with worked examples (bot vs human scenarios);
      repeat-offender pipeline (BAN_ESCALATION/CAP + BAN_ESCALATE_AFTER/WINDOW)
      grouped with scenario examples; BAN_ESCALATION value "exponential" renamed
      to "double" (old value still accepted); 4 internal-only variables
      (LOCK_FILE_TIMEOUT, OUTPUT_SYSLOG_FILE, BAN_RETRY_COUNT, LOG_SOURCE)
      moved to internals.conf with backward-compatible defaults
[New] bfd.lib.sh: 120-function library extracted from bfd for testability
[New] extract_hosts() declarative rule engine with fail2ban-compatible <HOST>
      patterns, dual IPv4/IPv6 boundary-aware regex, and IGNOREREGEX per-rule
      exclusion; all 34 rules converted from ad-hoc grep/sed/awk pipelines
[New] 22 new service rules (42 total): apache-auth, nginx-http-auth,
      mysqld-auth, wordpress, webmin, directadmin, cyrus-imap, roundcube,
      plesk, dropbear, http_401, pam_generic, named, postgresql,
      openvpn, phpmyadmin, gitlab, grafana, proxmox, lighttpd, mongodb, xrdp
[New] pressure.conf: centralized per-rule pressure configuration
      (PRESSURE_WEIGHT, PRESSURE_TRIP, SKIP_ALERT, RULE_EMAIL); three-tier
      precedence: rule file > pressure.conf > conf.bfd; replaces thresholds.conf
[New] _rule_tlog() in-process tlog wrapper replaces $TLOG_PATH subprocess in
      all 34 rules; eliminates 34 fork+exec pairs per detection cycle
[New] pressure-to-response model: exponential-decay scoring replaces fixed
      count thresholds; events add weighted pressure (PRESSURE_WEIGHT per rule),
      pressure decays via half-life (PRESSURE_HALF_LIFE, default 300s), bans
      fire when accumulated pressure exceeds trip point (PRESSURE_TRIP, default
      20); PRESSURE_TRIP_GLOBAL cross-service aggregate trip (0=off);
      all math in native awk floats with scaled-integer bash comparison;
      backward compat: old TRIG/TRIG_WINDOW configs auto-migrate
[New] country pressure multipliers: auto-enabled when pressure-country.conf
      has entries; IP-to-country lookup via ipcountry.dat (binary-search on
      sorted integer ranges); pressure-country.conf maps country codes to
      multipliers (20=2.0x, 10=1.0x); pressure_effective_weight() scales
      per-rule weight by country factor
[New] distributed attack detection: SUBNET_TRIG unique IPs from same subnet
      triggers subnet ban; ip_to_subnet() with configurable IPv4/IPv6 masks
[New] FIREWALL="auto" with 8 backends (APF, CSF, firewalld, UFW, nftables,
      iptables, route, custom); auto-detection in priority order;
      fw_ban/fw_unban/fw_setup/fw_status dispatch layer; nftables sets,
      iptables chain, firewalld rich rules, route blackhole
[New] full IPv6 support: dual-stack detection, banning, and local address
      exclusion; BAN_COMMAND_V6/UNBAN_COMMAND_V6 for firewalls requiring
      separate commands; validate_ip6() with zone ID stripping
[New] temporary bans with auto-expiry (BAN_TTL, default 600s); recidivism
      escalation (BAN_ESCALATE_AFTER/BAN_ESCALATE_WINDOW); ban escalation modes
      (BAN_ESCALATION: none/linear/double, BAN_ESCALATION_CAP);
      execute_ban/execute_unban with retry and exponential backoff; old names
      (BAN_DURATION, BAN_PERMANENT_AFTER/WINDOW) accepted via silent fallback
[New] bans.active and bans.history state files with atomic flock -x appends;
      $PORTS substitution for port-specific blocking
[New] batched email alerts: single email per recipient per check cycle with
      enriched content (ban type, duration, recidivism, log excerpts);
      RULE_EMAIL per-rule routing; SKIP_ALERT per-rule suppression
[New] CLI expanded from 4 to 21 flags: -S/--status, -C/--config, -R/--rules,
      -T/--test, --test-pattern, -l/--list, -u/--unban, -b/--ban, -c/--check,
      -d/--dryrun, -w/--watch, -V/--verbose, -v/--version, -h/--help,
      --flush-temp, --flush-all, --json, --csv
[New] -w/--watch continuous daemon mode (WATCH_INTERVAL, default 10s); SIGHUP
      config reload; bfd-watch.service (systemd) and bfd-watch.init (SysVinit
      for CentOS 6 / Ubuntu 14.04); dead-PID lock recovery for cron fallback
[New] -V/--verbose flag with vout() instrumentation across check, unbans,
      status, and health check
[New] -c/--check health check: validates config, log paths, firewall binaries,
      rule status, state directories, tlog, and active bans
[New] detect_run_mode() for structured run-mode identification (watch/systemd,
      watch/init, watch/manual, timer/systemd, cron, unknown)
[New] systemd journal reader with transparent fallback (16 of 34 rules);
      LOG_SOURCE config (auto/file/journal); cursor-based journal tracking
[New] conf.bfd reorganized into 6 sections; internals.conf split out;
      validate_config() checks 24 variables at startup with clear error
      messages and meaningful exit codes
[New] bfd.1 nroff man page (OPTIONS, CONFIGURATION, PRESSURE MODEL, FIREWALL,
      RULES, FILES, SIGNALS, EXIT CODES); installed via install.sh
[New] bfd.bash-completion: context-sensitive tab completion for all CLI flags,
      IPs, rule names, config variables, and file paths
[New] importconf rewritten: awk-based config merge preserving user values;
      TRIG→PRESSURE_TRIP migration in conf.bfd; thresholds.conf→pressure.conf
      per-rule translation; pre-2.0.1 backward compat (FIREWALL="custom");
      temp file cleanup trap
[New] install.sh: custom paths (INSTALL_PATH/BIN_PATH env vars); man page,
      bash completion, and SysVinit init script installation; post-install
      watch mode recommendation; stats/ mkdir
[New] uninstall.sh: root check; service stop ordering; man page, completion,
      init script, and backup directory cleanup
[New] safe_source() validates root ownership and non-world-writable permissions
      before sourcing; expand_command_template() and sanitize_ports() for safe
      template expansion without eval
[New] validate_ip()/validate_ip6()/validate_ip_any() strict IP validation;
      sanitize_mod() restricts rule names to safe characters
[New] record_ban(), _save/_restore/_clear_rule_vars(), _rule_is_active()
      helpers consolidating duplicated logic across callers
[New] bfd.service, bfd.timer, bfd-watch.service systemd units with
      SyslogIdentifier
[New] .shellcheckrc and full shellcheck compliance across all scripts
[New] .github/workflows/ci.yml with 8-OS Docker matrix and Buildx caching
[New] BATS test suite: 929 tests across 31 .bats files; shared helpers
      (assert-bfd.bash, bfd-mock.bash, bfd-common.bash); parallel runner;
      9 Dockerfiles; RFC 5737 test IPs throughout; dedicated pressure model
      and country multiplier test suites
[Change] check() rewritten: pressure-based scoring via record_and_score()
         replaces count_failures(); per-rule weight/trip/half-life; optional
         country multipliers; global cross-service pressure trip; per-run
         statistics; duplicate-ban prevention via state_bans_active_check()
[Change] tlog modernized: cat subprocesses → read builtin; getsize() pre-
         create block eliminated (prevents double-read race); growth condition
         simplified; convergence with tlog_read() documented
[Change] shell modernization across all files: backticks → $(), $[expr] →
         $(( )), egrep → grep -E, for-cat → while-read, systematic variable
         quoting, hardcoded paths → command -v discovery
[Change] -a/--attackpool extended with search_ip() report, per-service
         breakdown, and ban status integration
[Change] logrotate.d.bfd rewritten: copytruncate, weekly, compress, create 0640
[Change] cron.daily: flock-wrapped state rotation; copy-and-truncate preserves
         inodes; INSTALL_PATH variable; cursor files preserved; GPL header added
[Change] README wholesale rewrite: quick start, config reference, rule catalog,
         ban lifecycle, firewall backends, IPv6, CLI flags, troubleshooting
[Change] default cron interval reduced from 3 to 2 minutes
[Change] version 1.6-1 → 2.0.1; copyright years updated to 2026
[Fix] security: alert eval echo injection replaced with expand_command_
      template(); show_config() eval injection guarded by whitelist;
      BAN_COMMAND template extracted raw preventing premature expansion;
      custom backend PORTS validated via sanitize_ports()
[Fix] security: safe_source() applied to all sourced files (bfd.lib.sh,
      conf.bfd, alert.bfd, rules, tlog); state file operations wrapped in
      flock -x; mktemp replaces PID-based temp files; state files created 600;
      tlog gunzip/gzip race replaced with zcat
[Fix] global lock: FD-based flock replaced with mkdir-based lock eliminating
      eval "exec $LOCK_FD" and fd-0-close risk; PID liveness check clears dead
      holder immediately for cron recovery
[Fix] install.sh: daemon-reload after sed; BINPATH parent dir creation; CWD
      portability; chmod 640 for sourced files via find -type f; stats/ mkdir
      with chmod 750; no-op sed target removed
[Fix] validate_config(): added OUTPUT_SYSLOG, EMAIL_ADDRESS, BFD_LOG_PATH,
      BAN_RETRY_COUNT, EMAIL_LOGLINES validation; header comment updated
[Fix] show_config(): BAN_COMMAND vars added to whitelist with _TEMPLATE mapping
[Fix] rule variable leakage: IGNOREREGEX/PORTS/SKIP_ALERT/RULE_EMAIL now
      properly reset between rules via _clear/_save/_restore helpers
[Fix] CLI exit codes: all dispatch branches validate args and propagate via
      || exit "$?"; unknown flags exit non-zero
[Fix] firewall backends: hardcoded paths replaced with command -v discovery
      for apf, csf, iptables, ip6tables, ip (route backend); CIDR addresses
      pass through without extra /32 or /128 suffix
[Fix] tlog: log rotation duplicate output; source safety validation;
      indentation normalized; idioms and version string updated
[Fix] rule fixes: postgresql impossible path test; vsftpd2 TLOG_TF collision;
      modsec FILE→LP rename; missing SKIP_ALERT in postfix/proftpd;
      ignore.hosts missing ::1 loopback
[Fix] IPv6: grep -Fw false-match replaced with awk/grep -Fx exact matching
[Fix] journal: tlog_journal_filter rh_ipop3d key mismatch; dispatch bypassed
      existing log files
[Fix] miscellaneous: POSIX == → = in [ ] tests; $EXIT_* quoting; _hc_config()
      eval → case; _apool_report() date -d fallback; -q subprocess → exec;
      attack pool regex → grep -F; local address grep -Ew fix; WATCH_INTERVAL
      ${-} → ${:-}; sed -r → sed -E; $! quoting; UNBAN_COMMAND warning gated
      on FIREWALL="custom"; firewalld examples removed --permanent flag
[Fix] pressure alerts: format_alert_body read 11 fields from 12-field alert
      file; weight field absorbed into half-life, corrupting email display;
      check_distributed normalized to 12-field format for consistency
[Fix] tab completion: bfd.bash-completion config_vars used old variable names
      (TRIG, BAN_DURATION, THRESHOLDS_CONF); updated to match show_config()
      whitelist (PRESSURE_TRIP, BAN_TTL, PRESSURE_CONF)
[Fix] display fallback: 5 display functions used hardcoded trip default of 15
      instead of documented default 20 (unreachable in practice)
[Fix] show_status rounding: awk int(p*1000+0.5) rounding inconsistent with
      pressure_compute printf truncation; normalized to truncation
[Fix] reload_watch: SIGHUP config reload did not clear derived pressure vars
      before re-sourcing, causing stale values when users edit legacy names
[Fix] ATTACK_COUNT backward compat: send_alerts set to raw pressure_scaled
      (e.g., 18400); now uses pressure/1000 for sensible old-template display
[Change] test infrastructure: adopt batsman shared BATS framework via submodule
      at tests/infra (pinned to 1.0.1); 9 Dockerfiles reduced from full OS+BATS
      install to single-package delta over batsman base images; run-tests.sh
      replaced with 21-line batsman wrapper; Makefile replaced with 8-line
      parameterized include; CI test job uses batsman reusable workflow
[Change] remove legacy run_tests.sh pre-BATS test runner

